WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.128
Hi, I'm Toggle!

00:00:02.128 --> 00:00:04.083
These agents get root inside a sandbox.

00:00:04.083 --> 00:00:07.435
Here is how the host and the keys stay out of reach.

00:00:10.017 --> 00:00:10.635
The idea.

00:00:10.635 --> 00:00:14.343
Each task gets a small virtual machine, and its network and keys

00:00:14.343 --> 00:00:15.888
are handled from outside it.

00:00:19.042 --> 00:00:22.043
The agent has root, but only over a guest kernel that

00:00:22.043 --> 00:00:23.135
nothing else depends on.

00:00:23.555 --> 00:00:27.543
Below it, Firecracker runs in a jail, with its own user and

00:00:27.543 --> 00:00:29.205
namespaces and hard resource limits.

00:00:29.625 --> 00:00:31.830
Only then the hardware boundary and the host.

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:37.063
Every connection from the guest goes to a gateway that serves only

00:00:37.063 --> 00:00:38.527
this sandbox, on the host.

00:00:38.947 --> 00:00:40.397
It checks the policy.

00:00:40.397 --> 00:00:42.935
Metadata and private ranges are always denied.

00:00:43.355 --> 00:00:46.448
If a rule's host, path and method match, the gateway adds the

00:00:46.448 --> 00:00:47.737
key on the way out.

00:00:47.737 --> 00:00:49.026
The guest never sees it.

00:00:50.608 --> 00:00:52.386
A sandbox outlives its request.

00:00:53.197 --> 00:00:55.641
Running: live memory and a copy-on-write disk.

00:00:56.061 --> 00:00:58.197
Paused: memory stays on the worker.

00:00:58.197 --> 00:00:59.264
Fast, not durable.

00:00:59.684 --> 00:01:02.889
Suspended: dirty memory and changed disk go to storage.

00:01:03.309 --> 00:01:06.402
Forked: frozen, captured, restored as a new sandbox.

00:01:08.008 --> 00:01:09.205
Then they attacked it.

00:01:09.205 --> 00:01:12.197
Nine model setups with root tried for a host secret.

00:01:12.197 --> 00:01:14.590
No escape in one hundred and eight runs.

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:18.830
With some network allowed, agents slipped past the egress rules in eleven

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:21.058
of fifty four runs, before the fix.

00:01:22.758 --> 00:01:25.781
Zero of one hundred and eight is not a proof.

00:01:25.781 --> 00:01:28.200
Generously, it bounds the rate near three percent.

00:01:30.558 --> 00:01:31.160
The takeaway.

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:32.665
The machine guards the host.

00:01:32.665 --> 00:01:36.276
The network and keys are a separate boundary, and that one broke.

00:01:39.525 --> 00:01:40.270
To recap.

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:44.370
One jailed machine per task, keys attached outside, and sandboxes that

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:45.861
pause, suspend and fork.

00:01:46.281 --> 00:01:48.373
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:48.373 --> 00:01:48.971
I'm Toggle.

00:01:48.971 --> 00:01:49.270
Bye!
